{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786281535,"nonce":"scHwtRGETfVgLEs4o6Z0GhBeXJA=","title":"**What is wrong.** Six tables stamp `created_at` and `updated_at` from the Go clock on","message":"INSERT and then write a plain `updated_at = $n` on UPDATE, with a `\u003ctable\u003e_time_ck`\ncomparing the two: `clusters`, `alert_sources`, `notification_policies`,\n`notifications`, `notification_deliveries` and `channel_threads`.\n\nThat is internally consistent on the database-clock-versus-app-clock axis, which is\nwhat the survey in `becd24b` checked and cleared. It is not safe on the axis that\nsurvives: **oto runs N pods with N clocks.** The pod issuing the UPDATE is frequently\nnot the pod that ran the INSERT, and a few milliseconds of lag between them writes an\n`updated_at` below `created_at` and trips the CHECK — a 23514 surfacing as a 500, with\nnothing actually wrong.\n\nThis is the same defect already fixed on `channels` (`becd24b`), `orgs` and\n`channel_credentials` (`994e334`). The fix there was `GREATEST(updated_at, $n)`, which\nmakes the column monotonic and cannot regress a legitimate write.\n\n**Why it matters.** `notification_deliveries` is the most exposed: the INSERT and the\nfirst status update are both on the hot delivery path and are frequently different\npods. A 500 there is a delivery that appears to have failed for no reason — and\nCONTEXT.md §6 requires that delivery failure be visible per alert, so a spurious one is\nworse than a silent one. `channel_threads` carries the Slack thread binding.\n\nThis was found while fixing `orgs`, not by any gate. Nothing in CI catches it, and it\nonly reproduces under real clock skew between pods, so it will not show up in a\nsingle-process test run.\n\n**Where.** `internal/sources/repository/`, `internal/notification/repository/`\n(`policies.go`, `notifications.go`, `deliveries.go`, `threads.go`),\n`internal/identity/repository/` — every UPDATE writing `updated_at` on the six tables\nnamed above. `internal/notification/repository/threads.go` `OrderingStore.Advance` is\nalready correct and is the reference.\n\n**Done when.** Every UPDATE against a table with a `created_at`/`updated_at` CHECK\nwrites `updated_at` monotonically, and a regression test with a clock behind the row's\ncreator proves it, in the style of\n`internal/channels/repository/channels_clock_test.go`.","files":null}]}